Local patch for OpenStack Trove: Percona datastore validation-rules.json
(targets trove/templates/percona/validation-rules.json; branch stable/2026.1).

Why this patch is needed
------------------------
Trove ships trove/templates/percona/validation-rules.json, the allow-list of
configuration parameters a user may set on a `percona` datastore instance via
`openstack database configuration`. The upstream file is a stale ~36-parameter
subset (a strict subset of upstream's own MySQL 8.4 rules) and omits the
parameters Percona Server 8.4 actually accepts, so users are wrongly blocked
from tuning valid variables.

What this changes
-----------------
Rebuilds the file as a Percona Server 8.4 rule set (132 parameters) from
authoritative sources only -- the legacy Percona 8.0 rule set is intentionally
NOT used:

  * Base (102 params): the UNION of upstream Trove's MySQL 8.4 rules
    (trove/templates/mysql/validation-rules.json) and upstream's Percona rules
    (trove/templates/percona/validation-rules.json). Percona Server 8.4 is a
    drop-in fork of Oracle MySQL 8.4, so every MySQL 8.4 parameter is valid on
    Percona 8.4; upstream's percona file is a subset and adds nothing, so the
    union equals the MySQL 8.4 set. Every one of these is guaranteed-valid.

  * Plus (30 params): Percona Server 8.4 enhancements that exist in neither
    upstream file -- thread pool (thread_pool_*), user/table/index statistics
    (userstat, thread_statistics), enhanced slow-query log (log_slow_*),
    audit log plugin (audit_log_*), and InnoDB/transaction extensions
    (innodb_kill_idle_transaction, innodb_show_verbose_locks, ...).

Review note (upstream PR / follow-up JIRA)
------------------------------------------
The 30 Percona-only entries carry documented types and conservative bounds /
restart_required flags, but have NOT yet been verified against a running
Percona Server 8.4. Exact min/max and dynamic-vs-static behaviour can vary by
point release. Before this merges upstream, regenerate/confirm these from a
live percona/percona-server:8.4 instance (SHOW VARIABLES +
performance_schema.variables_info). The 102-parameter base needs no such check
(it is upstream MySQL 8.4, already validated).

Applies from the trove repo root with `git apply -p1` or `patch -p1`.

